

Google Apps Script Helper

onOpen()
      
      Runs automatically when the spreadsheet is opened.
      
      Creates two custom menus in the Google Sheets UI: "Generate Status" and "Generate Approval/Disapproval Page", allowing users to manually trigger scripts.
      
      runAutomatedProcess(), runAutomatedProcessone(), runAutomatedProcesstwo()
      
      These are functions scheduled to run automatically at different times of the night.
      
      They execute the three main status-checking scripts (checkApprovalStatus, findFirstDisapprovingSheet, and findFirstDisapprovalReason) to update the master sheet without manual intervention.
      
      PDF Generation & Emailing

approvesda()

    Generates a formatted PDF "Approval Page" for memos marked "APPROVED" or "PENDING" (under certain conditions).
    
    The PDF includes memo details, approver names, their digital signatures, and timestamps.
    
    Saves the PDF to a specific Google Drive folder and puts a link to it in the main "Conso" sheet.

disapproveds()
    
    Functions similarly to approvesda but only for memos marked "DISAPPROVED".
    
    It creates a "Disapproval Page" PDF that shows the memo details and the reviewers' comments/statuses.

sendApprovalEmails()

    Scans for "APPROVED" memos that have not been notified yet.
    
    Sends a formatted HTML email to the uploader/preparer, informing them of the approval.
    
    Logs the email details in an "EMAIL SUMMARY" sheet to prevent duplicates.

senddispprovalEmails()

    Identical to the function above but for memos marked "DISAPPROVED".
    
    Sends a notification email about the disapproval.
    
    Optimized Data Processing

checkApprovalStatus_Optimized()
    
    A high-performance function that determines the final status ("APPROVED", "PENDING", or "DISAPPROVED") for each memo.
    
    It does this by efficiently checking the status across all individual approver sheets and applying the business rules.

findFirstDisapprovingSheet_Optimized()

    An efficient function that scans all related approver sheets to find the name of the first person who disapproved a memo.
    
    It updates the "Conso" sheet with the name of that person.

findFirstDisapprovalReason_Optimized()

    A fast function that finds the specific comment or reason provided by the first person who disapproved the memo.
    
    It writes this remark into the "Conso" sheet.
    
    Helper Functions

getTimestampFromSheet(), getNotes(), getTimestampFromSheett(), getNotess()

    These are small, reusable helper functions.
    
    Their job is to look inside an individual approver's sheet and fetch specific information, like an approval/disapproval date or a remark, for a given memo.

